      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence (paper 2004.00809) fully supports the question. The Abstract states Twitter data makes better predictions about the inventory of languages used in each country (r=0.60 social media vs r=0.49 web-crawled for population correlation). Supporting details: Twitter provides better representation of North America and Oceania (Population Demographics section); Discussion finds diverging representations, fewer missing languages on Twitter ('In this case Twitter has fewer missing languages'), and more false positives in Twitter data. Collection details (50km radius of 10k cities, no language-specific keywords, May 2017–early 2019, ~1.066B tweets, 4.14B words) are also present. All claims are drawn directly from retrieved text, not commonsense."
      },
